            <ArticleTitle>Association analysis of polymorphisms in the interleukin-4 receptor (alpha) gene with atopic asthma in patients from western Mexico.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>375-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We undertook an association analysis between the ile50val, glu375ala, cys406arg, and ser761pro polymorphisms of the IL-4Ralpha gene and atopic asthma, total IgE levels and IL-4 serum levels in a population from western Mexico. We found that the ser761pro polymorphism was monomorphic for ser761, while there was no association between any of the other polymorphisms and the three phenotypes analysed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
